# The hospital's own archive. Real patient data belongs with the practice, not
# in a repository - the folder is tracked, its contents are not.
# Patient data, wherever it sits. The pattern used to be data/*.csv, which
# missed an identical copy of the archive sitting at the repository root - 984
# patient records that would have been committed. Anchor-free patterns here on
# purpose: a spreadsheet of patients is never safe to publish, whatever folder
# somebody drops it in.
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.dump
!data/README.md

.vercel
.env*

# Database dumps. They contain everything, including patient data.
backups/
